    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\"><span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span><span class=\"time\">40 min</span><span class=\"chip bad\">Hard</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Binary search</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Partition</span><a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/median-of-two-sorted-arrays/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 4</a></div>\n  <h1>Median of Two Sorted Arrays</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Insight in one line: do not merge, cut. Binary-search how many numbers the shorter array gives to the left half; the other array's count follows, and two cross checks say \"too many\" or \"too few\". O(log min(m, n)) time, O(1) space.</p>\n"
